+# Raumata dual-protocol stack
+
+This tree runs Meshtastic and MeshCore concurrently on the Heltec V3's single
+SX1262 so one radio can participate in both a Meshtastic mesh and a MeshCore
+mesh without a hardware modification.
+
+## Shared PHY profiles
+
+A LoRa receiver has one demodulator configuration at a time. Raumata keeps the
+SX1262 in **one selectable physical configuration (`PhyProfile`)** stored in NVS
+(`raumata/phy`) and shared by both stacks:
+
+- **Meshtastic presets** (`ANZ LongFast`, `ANZ MediumSlow`, `ANZ ShortFast`,
+  `US LongFast`, `EU868 LongFast`): native sync word `0x2B`, 16-symbol preamble,
+  region/channel frequency calculation.
+- **MeshCore presets** (`Australia (Narrow)` 916.575 MHz BW62.5/SF7/CR7,
+  `New Zealand (Narrow)` 917.375 MHz, `US/Canada (Narrow)` 910.525 MHz,
+  `Portugal 868` 869.618 MHz): native sync word `0x12`, 32-symbol preamble,
+  explicit frequency override.
+- **Dual presets** (`Dual AU (common 0x2B)` and `Dual AU (common 0x12)`):
+  explicit 916.575 MHz BW62.5/SF7/CR7 with a chosen common sync word.
+- **Custom (`255`)**: user-defined frequency, bandwidth, spreading factor,
+  coding rate, sync word, preamble length, and TX power.
+
+`raumata::phyInit()` loads the active profile before `initLoRa()` and drives
+both `config.lora` and `RadioInterface`'s `syncWord` and `preambleLength`.
+Runtime changes from either the Meshtastic radio configuration or the MeshCore
+companion API (`CMD_SET_RADIO_PARAMS`, `CMD_SET_RADIO_TX_POWER`,
+`CMD_SET_PHY_PROFILE`, or CLI `phy list|get|set`) reconfigure the radio once for
+both stacks and schedule a rate-limited re-advertisement.
+
+## Frame demultiplexing
+
+MeshCore frames are prepended with the four-byte transport tag `RAUM` before
+they reach the radio. Received frames beginning with the tag are stripped and
+handed to MeshCore; everything else is passed to Meshtastic unchanged. The tag
+is transport-level only, so MeshCore's packet format and cryptography are
+unmodified.
+
+## Radio ownership and shared airtime
+
+`RadioLibInterface` exposes a raw-frame sink and a raw transmit path:
+
+- **RX**: the sink runs after `readData()` and before Meshtastic header parsing.
+  MeshCore frames are queued for `MeshCoreRadio::recvRaw()`.
+- **TX & CAD**: MeshCore and Meshtastic serialize access with `rawRadioMutex`
+  and `sendingPacket`/`rawTxActive`/`isChannelBusy()`. `MeshCoreRadio` reports
+  channel busy whenever Meshtastic is transmitting or actively receiving a LoRa
+  frame, preventing TX-over-RX collisions.
+- **Airtime budget**: raw MeshCore transmissions are logged to Meshtastic's
+  `AirTime` tracker (`TX_LOG`), and `PresenceScheduler` scales the MeshCore
+  `Dispatcher` airtime budget factor to 25% of the regional duty cycle.
+
+## Dual identity, presence, and node features
+
+`src/raumata/MeshCoreNode.*`, `IdentityLink.*`, and `PresenceScheduler.*`
+implement a full `BaseChatMesh` companion node:
+
+- **Identity & Link Record**: Ed25519 keypair persisted in NVS (`raumata/mc_id`,
+  or deterministically derived via HKDF-SHA256 from the Meshtastic private key
+  when built with `-DRAUMATA_IDENTITY_DERIVED=1`), linked with the Meshtastic
+  `NodeNum` and Curve25519 public-key fingerprint in `raumata/link`.
+- **Name Synchronization**: defaults to Meshtastic `owner.long_name` /
+  `short_name` and tracks owner updates unless an explicit `raumata/mc_name`
+  override is set via `CMD_SET_ADVERT_NAME`.
+- **Presence**: staggered boot announcements (`T+15s` MeshCore advert, `T+20s`
+  Meshtastic `NodeInfo`) and 15-minute periodic adverts with deterministic
+  per-node jitter and GPS coordinates from `localPosition`.
+- **Persistence & Messaging**: up to 8 group channels (`raumata/mc_ch`) and 32
+  contacts (`raumata/mc_contacts`) persisted in NVS, direct and group text,
+  outbound ACK matching, push notifications (`PUSH_CODE_MSG_WAITING`,
+  `PUSH_CODE_SEND_CONFIRMED`, `PUSH_CODE_NEW_ADVERT`, `PUSH_CODE_ADVERT`,
+  `PUSH_CODE_PATH_UPDATED`), custom variables (`CMD_GET_CUSTOM_VARS`), and
+  core/radio/packet statistics (`CMD_GET_STATS`).
+
+## Companion interface
+
+A USB-serial mux parses both Meshtastic (`0x94 0xC3`) and MeshCore (`<`)
+framing. With `RAUMATA_COMPANION_MODE_BLE_USB=1` (enabled by default in
+`heltec-v3-dual`), USB starts in MeshCore companion mode so a Meshtastic app can
+connect over BLE while a MeshCore app connects over USB simultaneously without
+debug log or `FromRadio` queue contention.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+pio run -e heltec-v3-dual
+```
